  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- `IProcessingContext.RequestedVehicleProperties` selects which vehicle property groups Intrada calculates during processing; a group you do not request is calculated on first access instead.\n- The string form of `IntradaOptions` and of an `IIntradaAlpr` instance shows the licence key masked, so logging or printing them no longer writes the key.\n- A reference frame on an image wider than it is high is no longer rejected with `PointNotInImageException` under Intrada 7, and reads back with the width and height it was set with.\n- A complex area of interest that is not square no longer reaches Intrada transposed, under Intrada 6 and 7.\n- A complex area of interest whose cells the native library holds as values other than 0 and 1 is read back correctly when inverted.\n- Vehicle results report the detected vehicle types and the make/model pairs as collections, so alternatives such as `TRUCK|TRAILER`, or `VOLKSWAGEN|VOLVO` with `POLO|XC90`, no longer have to be taken apart by hand.\n- A `Package` set on `IntradaOptions` is now used when Intrada initialises; before, it was silently ignored.\n- Setting `Package` on an Intrada that cannot take one (Intrada 6, or Intrada 7 before 7.7) now raises an error. An empty `Package` is treated as no package.\n- Exceptions thrown for an Intrada error now carry Intrada's text for that error code, and the error log line shows that text instead of `[empty]`.",
  "verbatimVersion": "7.8.0",
